# 3. Different Shells

A shell is a program that interprets commands and allows the user to interact with the operating system.

| Shell | Operating System / Environment | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Bash | Linux, Unix, WSL | Common shell with scripting support |
| Zsh | macOS, Linux | Similar to Bash with additional customization |
| PowerShell | Windows, Linux, macOS | Administration shell using object-based pipelines |
| CMD | Windows | Older Windows command shell |
| WSL | Windows | Runs Linux environments and shells inside Windows |

Cloud command-line tools such as `aws` and `az`, and language interpreters such as Python and Node.js, are not themselves shells.

