# 21. Key Takeaways

1. CLI tools can be combined using pipes and redirection.
2. Bash pipelines pass text; PowerShell pipelines pass objects.
3. Globs match filenames, while regular expressions match text.
4. Quoting variables prevents unwanted word splitting and pathname expansion.
5. Scripts allow tasks to be automated and repeated.
6. Exit statuses help determine whether commands succeeded.
7. Commands involving deletion, permissions or elevated privileges can be dangerous.
8. Never blindly execute scripts downloaded from untrusted sources.
9. Use least privilege instead of unnecessarily running commands as root.
10. The command line is a practical tool for monitoring, administration, automation and cybersecurity investigations.

